<title>INDONESIA: Bank Indonesia says no clearing on Thursday.</title>
<headline>Bank Indonesia says no clearing on Thursday.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's central bank, Bank Indonesia, said there will be no clearing on Thursday due to voting in the general elections.</p>
<p>But it said foreign exchange transactions with the central bank will operate as usual.</p>
<p>Dealers said the absence of a clearing schedule will reduce market activity to a minimum.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom 384-6364</p>
</text>
